  "title": "Hearing intervals",
  "summary": "Tie each interval to a song you already know, so you can hear it without counting keys.",
  "minutes": 7,
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Songs you already know",
      "body": "Your ear already knows these intervals from songs. The opening notes of a familiar tune make a handy hook:\n\n- minor 2nd: the *Jaws* theme\n- major 2nd: *Happy Birthday*, from \"-py\" to \"birth\"\n- minor 3rd: *Greensleeves*\n- major 3rd: *Oh When the Saints*\n- perfect 4th: *Here Comes the Bride*\n- tritone: *The Simpsons* theme\n- perfect 5th: *Twinkle Twinkle Little Star*, the jump to the second \"twinkle\"\n- major 6th: *My Bonnie Lies Over the Ocean*\n- minor 7th: the original *Star Trek* theme\n- octave: *Somewhere Over the Rainbow*\n\nIf another song works better for you, use that one.",
      "exampleMidi": [
        60,
        61,
        62,
        63,
        64,
        65,
        66,
        67,
        69,
        70,
        72
      ],
